{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>From evening until morning.</b> Rashi explained: it must burn from evening until morning, and the Sages estimated this to be a half-log for the long nights of Tevet, and on short nights, if oil remains, it is of no concern. And it does not seem right to the Rav Yitzchak bar Avraham, of blessed memory, to always discard the leftover oil. Therefore he explained that according to the shortness of the nights they would make thick wicks so that no oil at all would remain for the next day. And so it implies in Menachot, which concludes: Ben Bibai was appointed over the *peka*. And this is the language of tractate Shabbat: from the worn-out breeches of the priests and from their turbans they would *make peki'ot* for wicks in the Temple."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The terms פקיע/פקיעות refer to twisted wick-cords; rendered with transliteration where the text uses the term as a technical noun, and rendered as a verb where the tractate Shabbat citation uses it in verbal form."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:13.039165092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}